Project 1

I have decided to put all resources and documentation in this file instead of on the individual
.cpp and .h files. This is to reduce clutter and improve organization.

Resources and documentation:
    W3 Schools
        Enum documentation: https://www.w3schools.com/cpp/cpp_enum.asp
    CPlusPlus.com
        Fstream::get documentation: https://cplusplus.com/reference/istream/istream/get/token
        String class documentation: https://cplusplus.com/reference/string/string/
    Stack Overflow
        Solution for checking eof with getline: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2251433/checking-for-eof-in-stringgetline

How to compile:
    1. make sure you are in the "Gavin-Dennis-P1/" directory
    2. in the terminal, run the "make" command to compile the programs
    3. Optionally, run the following commands to execute the program with the following
       test cases:
    * make test - runs P1 with tests/P1_test (a file that doesn't exist) as an argument
	* make test1 - runs P1 with tests/P1_test1 as argument
	* make test1e - runs P1 with tests/P1_test1e as argument
	* make test2 - runs P1 with tests/P1_test2 as argument
	* make test3 - runs P1 with tests/P1_test3 as argument
	* make test4 - runs P1 with tests/P1_test4 as argument
	* make testGavin - runs P1 with tests/P1_testGavin as argument
    4. the finished executuble 'P1' can be found in the 'build' directory (Gavin-Dennis-P1/build/)

Test cases:
    P1_test1.txt - one valid token 
    P1_test1e.txt - one invalid token 
    P1_test2.txt - a list with at least one of each token type, separated by spaces/new lines 
    P1_test3.txt - similar to test2 but with the whitespaces removed 
    P1_test4.txt - similar to test2 but with comments and blank lines added 
	P1_testGavin - my personal test case, longer and more complicated than the previous

    Tests 2, 3, and 4 are different, but should yield the same output with the exception
    of the line number.